Ticket **#4471** merged **412** reports about wrong booking dates. The desk marked the incident
**known** and queued one parser fix. Re-reading the export shows **two causes** in that merge —
only one belongs on #4471.

<Callout>
GitHub tickets [parser · 379](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) and
[hint · 33](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) are **closed** on the desk queue.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Filed tickets

| Cause | Reports | GitHub | Belongs on #4471? |
|-------|--------:|--------|-------------------|
| `parser` | **379** | [issue #1](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) | yes — month-first parser vs day-first tenants |
| `hint` | **33** | [issue #2](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) | no — booking-v3 **MM/DD/YYYY** hint on day-first locales |

The `hint` rows were merged into #4471 before anyone split them. They need their own fix and
should not wait on the parser queue alone.

## Lessons

- Count causes before you merge, not only subjects.
- Intake tags (`parser` / `hint`) are guesses; tenant locale and form version decide the cause.

